EXT. SINKING FISHING TRAWLER - DECK - DAWN

The boat tilts at ten degrees. Gray water sloshes at the rails. A radio mast leans.

CAPTAIN IMELDA DRAGOMIR, 50s, leathery, in yellow oilskins, stands at the wheelhouse door, counting heads with her finger. DEACON PRICE, 20s, deckhand, drags a blue cooler across the planks. OLU ABIODUN, 40s, engineer, slumps against a winch, hands black with oil. SANTIAGO "SANTI" VEGA, 30s, cook, bails with a saucepan. A girl, LIN HUANG, 12, the captain's niece, sits cross-legged on a coil of rope with a life vest two sizes too big.

IMELDA
Raft's inflated. Ten minutes.

DEACON
We said that twenty minutes ago.

OLU
Pump's dead.

SANTI
Saucepan's not.

Lin tightens a strap. Nobody hurries. Imelda hands Lin a granola bar.

IMELDA
Eat. It's a long wait.
